ed.", 70.32, 70.62]], "segments": [[0.0, 3.2, "I'd wake up at 3 AM with scratches across my arms,"], [3.38, 5.52, "and I hadn't even felt myself doing it."], [5.8, 8.08, "And there's a difference between seasonal allergies"], [8.08, 11.08, "and waking up at 47 covered in hives"], [11.08, 12.98, "you've never had before in your life."], [13.2, 16.02, "I switched my detergent, I tried antihistamines,"], [16.26, 18.76, "my doctor shrugged and said it was probably stress."], [19.1, 21.36, "None of it explained why this started now."], [21.66, 25.24, "Something changed, and I couldn't stop asking, why now?"], [25.52, 27.34, "One thing I'd never thought to look at"], [27.34, 28.74, "was what I was sleeping on."], [28.74, 31.26, "Dust mites live deep inside mattress foam."], [31.46, 34.34, "Their allergens can trigger reactions in sensitized people."], [34.56, 36.92, "Though what's driving any individual's symptoms"], [36.92, 39.14, "is something only a doctor can work out."], [39.26, 40.94, "I'm not saying that's everyone's answer."], [41.16, 42.26, "I'm still working with mine."], [42.52, 44.9, "But capture cards gave me one physical thing"], [44.9, 46.18, "I could actually do."], [46.4, 48.64, "A plant-derived lure draws mites in."], [48.9, 49.9, "They stick to the adhesive."], [50.2, 52.66, "You place four cards under the corners of your mattress,"], [52.98, 54.92, "weave them up to 90 days, then discard."], [54.92, 59.86, "In lab testing, capture cards captured up to 99% of dust mites."], [59.96, 62.06, "It's not a cure, it's ruling something out."], [62.3, 64.44, "And that felt like the first concrete step"], [64.44, 65.64, "I could actually take."], [65.8, 67.6, "See capture cards at the link below."], [67.84, 70.62, "90-day money-back guarantee, no return required."]]}